{
  "format": "contentrain-redirect-parity@1",
  "origin": "https://example.test",
  "about": "Redirection (John Godley) rules → RawRedirect / RawRedirectExcluded, as both @contentrain/wp-import (over REST) and the Contentrain Bridge (its tables) export them. Owned by wp-import; the Bridge copies this file unchanged and pins the commit it copied.",
  "rules": [
    "`groups` and `items` are Redirection's own rows (its tables' columns; REST items carry the same values). `action_data` is the target URL for a url action, the condition's data otherwise; `match_data` is the rule's own flags or null. `options` is the site's saved redirection_options, or null when never saved. The plugin is active.",
    "Flags a rule is matched with (Red_Source_Flags): query `exact`, case- and slash-sensitive; options never saved (a fresh install) ignore case and trailing slash; the saved options, then the rule's own `match_data.source`, override. Only valid values count: query exact|ignore|pass|exactorder, case and trailing booleans. A regex rule matches its query exactly; `exactorder` is written `exact`. Every rule, excluded ones too, carries `query`, `case_insensitive` and `trailing_slash`.",
    "An enabled rule in an enabled group with a url action and url match is served: `to` root-relative when on `origin`, else absolute; a status outside 3xx becomes 301 with a `status_note`. An error action with 410 or 451 is served too, `to` empty. A disabled rule or group, any other action (reason `not-a-redirect:<action>`, with its status) and any other match (reason `conditional-match:<match>`, with its `condition` and status) are excluded, with no `to`. `served_by` names a group's Apache (2) or nginx (3) module.",
    "`redirects` and `excluded` are each ordered by id as strings (`redirection:10` before `redirection:2`); `rules` is how many the source holds. Keys are compared order-free.",
    "`options: null` is what the Bridge reads as no saved option; over REST, `redirection/v1/setting` returns the fresh-install values merged the same way, so the expected output is one. A case with `only: 'rest'` (`options: 'unreadable'`: the settings endpoint refused) is wp-import's alone: a rule's flags are written only where the rule states them, a regex rule's query always `exact`. The Bridge always reads its options and skips it."
  ],
  "groups": [
